  "body": "Production has PayPal webhook intake enabled from the approved September 10 rollout, but the startup schema verifier still requires that gate to be disabled. Consequently, a subsequent release or restart fails verification even when every migration is already applied. This blocked the requester-name backend deployment from #405.\n\nAllow the existing PayPal webhook gate to retain either configured state. Continue requiring all four provider gates to exist and requiring PayPal refunds and both Datafast gates to remain disabled. This changes no feature-flag values, migration files, or payment handlers.\n\nValidation:\n- 60 release/entrypoint tests and 21 CI contract tests passed.\n- Isolated PostgreSQL production fixture: applied the complete main migration bundle twice, preserved enabled PayPal intake on the second run, and rejected all four missing-gate cases plus all three unauthorized-enabled-gate cases.\n- The same focused verifier correction passed against the deployed backend schema in a read-only transaction (`BEGIN READ ONLY; ... ROLLBACK;`). No production data, flags, or Machines were changed.\n- Added the enabled-webhook restart and seven negative cases to the existing automatic-migration backend integration test; shell syntax and catalog audit passed.\n\nDeployment remains pending review. The requester-name runtime patch is separately based on the live backend commit, so it does not introduce the 12 unrelated migrations currently pending on main.\n\nProduction backport prepared at `954e995f1cd08f363afe2b0e34ccf02dcd80ea8c`; image checks: https://github.com/diegueins680/tdf-app/actions/runs/35139447940. No deployment has been executed.\n",
  "created_at": "2026-09-16T19:14:41Z",
